{{Term/Store|Mighty Bananas|Mighty Bananas|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI}}<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Spoils"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Mighty Bananas}}
Mighty Bananas can be found growing in the tropical forests of [[West Necluda]] and on [[Eventide Island]]. They are also sold by [[Emri]] in [[Kara Kara Bazaar]] and dropped by regular [[Hinox]]. Eating one raw heals half of a [[Heart]]. When [[Cooking|Cooked]], the resulting [[Meal]] provides [[Link]] with the [[Attack Up]] [[Added Effect]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> This is due to the high amount of protein and calories present that they contain.<ref name="BotW Nali"/> Mighty Bananas exposed to [[Fire]] become [[Roasted Mighty Bananas]]. They can be used at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] to make [[Yellow Dye]].

Mighty Bananas are one of three foodstuffs favored by the [[Sheikah]], with the others being [[Swift Carrot]]s and [[Fortified Pumpkin]]s. They are the clear obsession of the [[Yiga|Yiga Clan]], as the [[Yiga Clan Hideout]] contains many Mighty Bananas. In addition, all [[Yiga Footsoldier]]s and [[Yiga Blademaster]]s drop them upon their defeat. The Yiga Blademasters patrolling the Yiga Clan Hideout will also deviate from their path to eat Mighty Bananas that are left on the ground. [[Monk Maz Koshia]] will also stop fighting and eat them should Link drop some during their fight.

Mighty Bananas are required to make [[Fried Bananas]] in a [[Cooking Pot]].
